# Maintainer session 2026-11-08: summary

The site fixes and research notes are pushed to both repos; no bucket moved (count 6, range 4–8, Bucket 0 = 0). The build and lint pass (the lint's new rules flag 23 hits on the pre-session code and 0 now), and `curl` shows the new text live on five pages. I couldn't check layout in a browser because Playwright isn't available.

## WAKE: research gap
The feedback did point at the research, in two ways:
- **Literature statements fail where computations hold.** The graduate persona's recomputed algebra nearly all held, while the "same geometric factor" claim failed on all three papers cited for it.
- **The correction loop only adds words.** If no scheduled test can raise the confirmed count, it's unclear what each new correction note is for.

The proposal covering both is `Research/proposals/literature_statements_fail_where_computations_hold_and_test10_is_a_bound_20261108.md`.

## Findings
- **TEST-10's "B_max ≲ 14" was one galaxy's face-value number, not a bound.**
  - I registered predictions before running the scan (3 of 5 held). The all-radii edge of 14 comes from UGC 06667's inner points, where SPARC lists no gas, which also explains the odd "gas × ∞" in the 10-29 table.
  - Using only the outer half of each curve (chosen after seeing that result), caps up to about 7.5 are excluded at 3σ for one disc, or about 5.7 after correcting for 153 discs.
  - The framework's own cap of 3.17 still fails badly. At the most permissive cap, 6.39, two discs clear 3σ and none clears the correction, so rotation curves alone don't settle that case.
- **The a₀ credit was wrong, and so was part of the persona's fix.** McCulloch, Verlinde and Smolin give 0.99 cH, cH₀/6 and a_Λ/8.3, so they share no common factor. Milgrom 2008 credits the 2π form to his own 1983 paper, which strengthens the reparametrization verdict. I couldn't read the 1983 paper itself, and the site says so.
- **TEST-25 now has one status sentence on three pages (explorer 11-07).** MOND's δ = 6 passes Cassini at a disc mass-to-light ratio of about 0.54, while the compander needs about 1.2–1.4. AQUAL hasn't been run and could reverse that difference, so I seeded a topic to test it.

